{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1544651-how-to-surprise-hunters-in-a-chronicle","id":1544651,"title":"How to surprise Hunters in a chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-24T08:36:16-07:00","id":1544651,"title":"How to surprise Hunters in a chronicle","content":"I was thinking of how besides Werewolves, Gangrel and Life Mages can transform into wolves and can potentially be misidentified as Werewolves. Besides misidentified monsters, imagine the hunters encountering &quot;mutants&quot; aka Fomori for example a Fomori Family from the Freak Legion book for a &quot;The Hills Have Eyes&quot; type of encounter or maybe even discovering an entire Pentex conspiracy and eventually having to deal with a First Team sent to silence them? But if you want to get really out there maybe you could pit the hunters against Bygones or maybe even Gargoyle Creatures or a pack of Demonhounds from the Dark Ages book (the latter) and the Book of Storyteller Secrets (the former)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 10-26-2024, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T18:23:02-07:00","id":1544697,"title":"","content":"So... What's really your question? Cuz it seems you already answered yourself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T18:48:25-07:00","id":1544700,"title":"","content":"I want an opinion on my ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T13:27:18-07:00","id":1544917,"title":"","content":"So, anyone think these are good ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T13:38:49-07:00","id":1544920,"title":"","content":"If you really want to confuse hunters, have them go up against &quot;mutants&quot; and then find out that the &quot;mutations&quot; fade by about an hour after death, either because they were around the bodies or they found out from proper investigators afterward. The debates turned flame wars on Hunter-Net would be something to see as a few manage to discern that something left their targets after death, and that they may have been possessed. Claims of a coverup if the cell didn't stay, claims of &quot;you're lying!&quot; if they did. Great for conflict. Eventually, though, most of HN will probably have to come to grips with it, just like they had to come to grips with werewolves just up and disappearing without a trace and then reappearing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T15:36:14-08:00","id":1546158,"title":"","content":"What about Abominations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T16:58:49-08:00","id":1546163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1544651-how-to-surprise-hunters-in-a-chronicle?p=1546158#post1546158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Abominations?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're either cacklingly evil or hobbled by Harano. Also, having them show up in numbers can strain suspension of disbelief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T17:09:34-08:00","id":1546166,"title":"","content":"I know, it would just be encountering one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-29T06:07:59-08:00","id":1547302,"title":"","content":"What if they encounter the Society of Leopold or Government Agents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T20:01:23-08:00","id":1547530,"title":"","content":"The hunters encountering Technocracy Hit Marks could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T17:40:24-08:00","id":1547567,"title":"","content":"Now encountering Kuei-Jin, Hsien or a Skinwalker could be a really good idea for a story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T01:05:07-07:00","id":1549899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1544651-how-to-surprise-hunters-in-a-chronicle?p=1547530#post1547530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hunters encountering Technocracy Hit Marks could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is something I've been considering with my Hunter campaign; where the majority of what seems supernatural isn't happening, it's actually being perpetrated by Mages as a form of mass panic so all the signs/monsters/hauntings are misleading to the cell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26060-nuhxnger36","name":"NuHxnger36","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T19:00:23-07:00","id":1550181,"title":"","content":"A Hit Mark is basically an artificially created soldier made by the Technocracy, think of it like the Terminator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-04T16:42:08-07:00","id":1552064,"title":"","content":"I just had another idea. What if your Hunter cell goes to Japan and let's say that they've encountered the local Kuei-jin who are referred to as Gaki. But in another story set in Japan after this they come across another group of vampires called Gaki but the twist is that this time it's the Japanese bloodline of Cainites from First Edition called Gaki.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 07-04-2025, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-04T22:02:13-07:00","id":1552067,"title":"","content":"Hunters are unlikely to ever found out how any of their targets call themselves. And two groups of creatures using the same legendary name isn't really a big deal.<br /> <br /> Most of your ideas boil down to hunters finding a new splat. This isn't bad, but isn't a fleshed out idea, either. They can cross paths with anything.<br /> <br /> And for the Hit Mark: it's really hard to encounter one of those outside an open conflict between the Union and the Traditions, Hit Marks don't wander around. Almost any situation where hunters find a Hit Mark, regardless if they're Imbued or HH's hunters, they'll have their hands full with just surviving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-04T22:21:08-07:00","id":1552068,"title":"","content":"Unless one group is going for brat and the other is hungry ghost... they're both a general name for <a href=\"https://jisho.org/search/%E9%A4%93%E9%AC%BC%20%23kanji\" target=\"_blank\">hungry ghosts</a> in Japanese. In fact, most people would probably be hard pressed to not use gaki to refer to every vampire and harmful ghost that fits the description. It's not like you can capitalize words in speech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T06:00:26-07:00","id":1552071,"title":"","content":"I think the single most surprising entity my Hunter group encountered was the Mummy who ran a tech corp, whom they suspected to be a vampire. They had no idea how to deal with him nor if they even should deal with him at all because I made him true neutral, and it confused the hell out of them.<br /> <br /> What I mean to say is that in my experience, Hunters are more surprised/engaged when presented with something that doesn't neatly fit their definition of Monster rather than what those monsters are or think of themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T17:53:01-07:00","id":1552220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1544651-how-to-surprise-hunters-in-a-chronicle?p=1552068#post1552068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless one group is going for brat and the other is hungry ghost... they're both a general name for <a href=\"https://jisho.org/search/%E9%A4%93%E9%AC%BC%20%23kanji\" target=\"_blank\">hungry ghosts</a> in Japanese. In fact, most people would probably be hard pressed to not use gaki to refer to every vampire and harmful ghost that fits the description. It's not like you can capitalize words in speech.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I figured that they would refer to multiple hungry undead in such a manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 07-09-2025, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T17:08:25-08:00","id":1555037,"title":"","content":"What if the hunters find out about one of the Ferectoi and think it's the Anti-Christ? That would be funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T02:13:55-08:00","id":1555049,"title":"","content":"I would try stories about people with rare diseases. Check Blue Fugates as an example. The show &quot;1000 ways to die&quot; can give you also mamy good ideas. My favourite part of it is about a violin player. She was arogant, overconfident, generally not very likable. She was found dead at the bottom of the stairs on her on house, broken neck, but without any signs of violence. At first glance murder, maybe by a jealous competitor. I can't remember how it was discovered but it was declared an accident: she slipped on the carpet at first floor. But, as her hands were the vital part of her artistic career, she tried to protect them and not the head. I would also try stories with tough moral choices. I once run a story for W: tA based of Full Eclipse where Adam was Theurge Skin Dancer who created fomori from best cops (usually the most aggresive, but that's another story) and, if a cop was also a kinfolk, another Skin Dancer. He really wanted to help people and make the coty safe. He even killed one of the fomori who gone to far, which was a sign of his true intentions for the PCs but on the other hand made their lives a little tougher for a while. You know, someone killed a cop from a special unit and they were seen near them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T04:17:34-08:00","id":1555051,"title":"","content":"I personally think Benjamen Holmscroft, the founder of the Arcanum, could be a mummy. It\u2019s not hinted at at all in Apostates, but I did get that impression from reading some older books about the Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 11-13-2025, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T16:39:49-08:00","id":1555079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1544651-how-to-surprise-hunters-in-a-chronicle?p=1555051#post1555051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure where I should put this, but: does anyone else think Benjamen Holmscroft, the founder of the Arcanum, could be a mummy? It\u2019s not hinted at at all in Apostates, but I did get that impression from reading some older books about the Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original The Hunter's Hunted had the various Arcanum founders practicing hedge magic, specifically alchemy that extended their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T16:50:48-08:00","id":1555081,"title":"","content":"Also, a Mummy in WoD is something very, very specific, even before Mummy: the Resurrection.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if he feels like a receiver of the Spell of Life in any of its few iterations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T10:46:45-08:00","id":1555126,"title":"","content":"The easiest way to surprise Hunters in a Chronicle is for their latest adventure to be a genuinely harmless hoax in which a Real Estate Swindler is literally unmasked, that van full of meddlesome adolescents are genuinely groovy and the huge dog that thinks it\u2019s people is a genuinely Good Boy.<br /> <br /> So much harmless eccentricity might even cause World of Darkness Hunters the same world-shaking existential uncertainty endured by Lovecraftian investigators (Albeit for exactly the opposite reason).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}